        "key": "E",
        "text": "A Midsummer’s Dream  \n \nText 1  \nSocial media advertising is a type of digital marketing that utilizes social networks such as Facebook, Twitter, \nand Instagram to deliver advertisements to your target audience in a quick and effective way, to connect with \nyour consumers, and to boost your marketing campaign. \nBy leveraging various data sources, advertisers are able to hyper -target their audiences and deliver \npersonalized content on the demography and the users’ behaviour. With the social media, advertisers may see \nmore interactions and conversations. Social media advertisements are also cost-effective, offering the potential \nfor high rates of return. \nSocial media advertising is a must if you quickly want to reach new target markets. More and more companies, \nincluding the world's top performing brands, utilize social media to reach out to new customers. To keep up \nwith the competition, we need to learn how these ads work and how they can benefit your company.  \nBecause both the internet and content marketing are constantly evolving, there are many ways to go about \nadvertising strategy on social media platforms. You may choose platforms suitable to your typical   \nadvertisements and your audience.  \nWhen considering social media’s advertising options, such as which advertising platforms to use, remember \nthat each platform has its own audience. It means you need to choose who your customers are. If you are \nalready active on social media, pay attention to the   platforms that perform well and   organize your posts   the \nmost interactively to target best audience.   \nText 2  \nHow effective are advertisements on social media?  Today, social media advertisement is just one of the \nvarious ways to reach consumers, besides TV, print, podcast, out -list or other digital, guerrilla tactics, in an \ninexpensive way. In the world of advert ising, media is more fragmented than it has ever been. Just how \neffective is social media advertising?  26% of social media users say they tend to buy uncostly brands they \nsee advertised.  \nClearly, adverts are not the only way for consumers to discover brands. If you really want to make your social \nmedia advertising effective, it is crucial for you to get it right. Majorities of consumers visited a social network \npreviously.  Nonetheless, with so many social media advertisements saturating our feeds, standing out is the \nkey. \nSo, how can you exactly optimize the presence of your social media’s brand to inspire and engage your \naudience? Using the latest social media report, we set out to explore   these audiences. Around the world, 27% \nof social media users say that they use social platforms primarily to research and find out certain product and \nGen Z and millennials make up 68% of those users. That is not surprising given that they are among the \nheaviest users of social media globally. Unlike their older counterparts, who use so cial media, Gen Z spend \nless than 3 hours per day on various platforms. Here are three key things to keep in mind:  being more effective   \nfor more audience, making social media frictionless, and lastly using social media to inform. \n \nTryout Prosus INTEN \nLiterasi dalam Bahasa Inggris\n: 20\n: 20 menit\nPROSUS INTEN \nPENGENALAN SOAL UTBK"
